# The annotations of tape block 3: two bytes loaded into the ROM's ERR_SP $5C3D (kit/mkgame.py --part
# src/loader/errsp.json). Format: ../../../../docs/ann-format.md. Witness: c1 (work/stage1/c1).

@module errsptext ; ERR_SP's new value
@about Loader $5EF3 loads this block with LD-BYTES (IX $5C3D, DE 2, flag $FF; c1 between frames 246 and 361).

$5C3D w ErrSpValue ; ERR_SP = 1: the ROM's error stack pointer
> Tape block 3, `01 00`. Nothing in the game writes ERR_SP again: it is a loading check. Every pass of MainLoop $9858 reads the word and, unless it is 1, hangs in a JR to itself at $985E, so a copy of the game block without this block (ERR_SP left at the ROM's value) freezes on its first game pass. The ROM never uses ERR_SP after the loader (the game never returns to BASIC and never makes an error). With ERR_SP = 1 a ROM error would load SP = 1 at ERROR-3 $0058, and SET-STK's RET at $16D3 would pop $11AF from the ROM's bytes $0001-$0002: a crash (known only from the code). Witness: c1 L1, 14 873 212 reads of $5C3D over the eight builds (tools/l1count.py --reads 5C3D-5C3E), all by $9858.
